---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaBlock from "../components/CtaBlock.astro";
import { CHANNELS, getModules, moduleHref, pad, utm } from "../lib/course";

const modules = await getModules();
const labs = modules.filter((m) => m.data.lab);
const exercises = modules.filter((m) => !m.data.lab);
---

<Base
  title="The Failure Labs | AIR Course 001"
  description="Every Failure Lab in Course 001. Each one breaks the vendor agent in a specific, reproducible way against the deterministic fixture server, then makes you fix it."
  pageSlug="labs"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAILURE LABS</p>
      <h1>Break it on purpose, then fix it</h1>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          The labs are the spine of this course. Every one of them is reproducible against the
          deterministic fixture server, so the failure you hit is the same failure everyone else
          hits, on the same page, at the same step. Watch the lab first if the video has shipped,
          then read the module and do it yourself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Run the fixture server</h2>
      <pre>{`git clone https://github.com/ogkranthi/air-course-long
cd air-course-long && make fixtures   # serves deterministic vendor sites on :8001`}</pre>
      <p class="muted measure">
        Failure behaviour is configured per URL and per attempt in a <code>profile.yaml</code>,
        so "pricing returns 503 twice then 200" is one line rather than a code change. Later
        modules add profiles; the server itself does not change.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>The labs</h2>
      <ol class="labs">
        {
          labs.map((m) => (
            <li class="labs__row">
              <span class="labs__tag">LAB {pad(m.data.module)}</span>
              <span class="labs__title">{m.data.lab}</span>
              <span class="labs__links">
                <a href={moduleHref(m)}>Module {pad(m.data.module)}</a>
                {m.data.youtube ? (
                  <a href={utm(m.data.youtube, m.id, "watch")} rel="noopener">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span> Watch
                  </a>
                ) : (
                  <span class="is-pending">Watch (coming)</span>
                )}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="muted measure">
        {exercises.map((m) => `Module ${pad(m.data.module)}`).join(" and ")} carry written
        exercises instead of a lab: the twelve-scenario classification and the case-study
        extraction. Both are graded by you, and Module 10 makes you re-do the first one.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>The gauntlet</h2>
      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Module 12 runs every failure at once against your deployed agent: page-level faults,
          content sprawl, contradictions, an injected instruction, plus a redeploy mid-run. It
          is the exam, because reality does not schedule its failures.
        </p>
        <p>
          Results go into a public Field Report on GitHub with a scorecard, traces, and a
          post-mortem. The best submissions become <a href={utm(CHANNELS.podcast, "labs", "listen")} rel="noopener">FDE Talks</a> episodes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CtaBlock slot="footer-cta" pageSlug="labs" />
</Base>

<style>
  .labs {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .labs__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .labs__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    width: 5rem;
    flex: none;
  }
  .labs__title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    color: var(--fg);
    flex: 1 1 18rem;
  }
  .labs__links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .is-pending { color: var(--fg-muted); opacity: 0.55; }
</style>
